Now the only contestable Proposition in this Syllogism is the Major, which can be prov'd by no other Principle than this, That our Reason is the Measure of all Truth, and whose Proof must be in this Form, Whatever is above the Measure of all Truth is not to be believ'd as true;
But our Reason is the Measure of all Truth:
Therefore whatever is above our Reason is not to be believ'd as true.
